  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday through Friday)\nIssued at 130 PM CDT Sat Aug 15 2026\n\nAbove normal temperatures continue next week as the upper-level \nridge remains dominant over the region. Afternoon highs in the mid \n90s to low 100s can be expected each day this work week, with the \nhottest spots ranging from 105 to near 110 along the Rio Grande. \nUpslope flow and diurnal heating yields a low (~10%) chance of \nshowers and storms over the Davis Mountains on Monday, though the \nrest of the forecast area remains dry. Sinking motion under the \nridge keeps the remainder of the week dry areawide.\n  \nGreening",
